Subject: [PATCH 5/6] [clang] Do not require clang-repl for the test suites

clang/test and clang/unittests key off HAVE_CLANG_REPL_SUPPORT, which only
records whether the platform could host a REPL. Whether the tool is built
is CLANG_TOOL_CLANG_REPL_BUILD, applied by add_clang_subdirectory. This
toolchain switches the tool off, because clang-repl asks the linker to
re-export the MSVC C++ runtime ABI by name (__type_info_root_node,
std::nothrow, the operator new/delete set) and sprt keeps those in its own
inline namespace.

With the tool off, CLANG_INCLUDE_TESTS=On first fails to configure:

  CMake Error at cmake/modules/AddLLVM.cmake:2118 (add_dependencies):
    The dependency target "clang-repl" of target
    "check-clang-utils-update_cc_test_checks" does not exist.

and then fails to build, because clang/unittests/Interpreter links the same
re-export list:

  lld-link: error: <root>: undefined symbol: struct __type_info_node __type_info_root_node
  lld-link: error: <root>: undefined symbol: struct std::nothrow_t const std::nothrow

Key both off the target instead. clang/tools is added before clang/test and
clang/unittests, so the target is already known.

diff --git a/clang/test/CMakeLists.txt b/clang/test/CMakeLists.txt
index 286c9d40d..47e5e7900 100644
--- a/clang/test/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/clang/test/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -195,7 +195,12 @@ if(CLANG_ENABLE_STATIC_ANALYZER)
   endif()
 endif()
 
-if (HAVE_CLANG_REPL_SUPPORT)
+# HAVE_CLANG_REPL_SUPPORT only says the platform could support a REPL; whether the tool
+# is actually built is CLANG_TOOL_CLANG_REPL_BUILD, applied by add_clang_subdirectory in
+# clang/tools. Depend on the target only if it exists, or configuring with the tool
+# switched off fails outright ("The dependency target clang-repl does not exist").
+# clang/tools is added before clang/test, so the target is known by now.
+if (TARGET clang-repl)
   list(APPEND CLANG_TEST_DEPS
     clang-repl
     )
diff --git a/clang/unittests/CMakeLists.txt b/clang/unittests/CMakeLists.txt
index 54c781a35..9677a800b 100644
--- a/clang/unittests/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/clang/unittests/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -92,7 +92,10 @@ add_subdirectory(Frontend)
 add_subdirectory(Rewrite)
 add_subdirectory(Sema)
 add_subdirectory(CodeGen)
-if(HAVE_CLANG_REPL_SUPPORT)
+# Same distinction as in clang/test: HAVE_CLANG_REPL_SUPPORT is a platform capability,
+# CLANG_TOOL_CLANG_REPL_BUILD is whether the tool is built. These tests link the same
+# re-exported MSVC C++ runtime ABI the tool does, so they are only buildable where it is.
+if(TARGET clang-repl)
   add_subdirectory(Interpreter)
 endif()
 # FIXME: libclang unit tests are disabled on Windows due
